---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import Img from '../../components/Img.astro';
import Video from '../../components/Video.astro';

const palette = ['#362D23', '#68280D', '#322127', '#6C4947', '#97644C', '#9A724F'];
---
<CaseLayout
  slug="jdel"
  section="playground"
  eyebrow="Passion project · Beauty"
  title="JDel Fragrance"
  summary="The perfume brand I’ve dreamed about since I was a kid, named for my mom and me. I used AI image generation to take it from idea to a high-fidelity bottle."
  hero="/images/jdel/bottle.webp"
  heroAlt="Amber glass perfume bottle with a gold cap, pearl collar, woven leather handle, and a JDel hang tag on draped satin"
  snapshot={[
    ['Category', 'Fragrance'],
    ['My role', 'Brand, palette, typography, prompts'],
    ['Tools', 'AI image generation'],
    ['Status', 'Concept'],
  ]}
>
  <section id="story" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Fragrance and me">Fragrance and me</h2>
    <p>
      As a kid, my mom’s perfume collection made me feel like a kid in a candy store. My favorite was a bottle shaped
      like a kokeshi doll. Then came a high heel, a cat, and even an Eiffel Tower. When my mom finished a bottle, it
      joined my Barbie collection. Each one felt like a tiny masterpiece.
    </p>
    <p>
      That game turned into a real hobby: layering my own combinations and tailoring them to the season. In the fall,
      it’s Lush’s Sticky Dates, a hint of Calvin Klein’s Escape, and a rollerball from my mom’s collection.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also became a dream: my own perfume brand. I even have the name. <strong>JDel</strong> blends my name with my
      mom’s, a tribute to the women who made me who I am.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="process" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Process">The process</h2>
    <p>
      I wanted JDel to feel <strong>elegant and timeless</strong>, with warm brown tones and a bottle that draws you in,
      like the ones I collected. I hand-picked the palette and typography, then wrote those choices directly into my
      prompts and varied them until the renders felt cohesive and luxury-driven.
    </p>
    <ul class="swatches" aria-label="JDel palette">
      {palette.map((c) => <li style={`--sw:${c}`}><span>{c}</span></li>)}
    </ul>
    <div class="pal-vid"><Video name="jdel-palette" label="JDel brand palette card with six warm brown swatches, followed by a bottle sketch" caption="Palette card and the first bottle sketch." /></div>
  </section>

  <section id="why" class="case-section">
    <h2 data-short="Why it matters">Why it matters</h2>
    <p>
      JDel is how I practice brand concepting: story first, then palette and type, then product. It’s also how I use AI:
      as a tool I steer with deliberate design choices, which is something I write about in
      <a href="/playground/raised-on-the-blur">Raised on the Blur</a>.
    </p>
    <p>For now, <a href="/projects/releaf">ReLeaf Candles</a> is the first chapter. One day, JDel will be real too.</p>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>

<style>
  .swatches { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 24px 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 10px; }
  .swatches li { aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--sw); display: flex; align-items: flex-end; padding: 8px; }
  .swatches span { font-size: 0.72rem; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .pal-vid { max-width: 420px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .swatches { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
</style>
